2864000,18.21],[1785542400,16.68],[1788220800,18.05]]}],"frequency":"M"},{"id":"desp_yoy","label":"Despatch YoY %","series":[{"id":"yoy","name":"YoY change","units":"Per cent","pts":[[1654041600,19.96],[1656633600,8.1],[1661990400,1.8],[1664582400,-4.39],[1667260800,4.44],[1672531200,8.68],[1675209600,4.69],[1677628800,7.39],[1680307200,11.49],[1682899200,5.86],[1685577600,4.05],[1688169600,13.04],[1690848000,18.81],[1693526400,14.98],[1696118400,17.95],[1698796800,10.59],[1701388800,8.75],[1704067200,6.53],[1706745600,13.56],[1709251200,8.7],[1711929600,6.09],[1714521600,10.62],[1717200000,11.79],[1719792000,5.49],[1722470400,-6.23],[1725148800,5.48],[1727740800,6.66],[1730419200,4.34],[1733011200,6.94],[1735689600,6.95],[1738368000,0.87],[1740787200,5.59],[1743465600,2.94],[1746057600,-2.22],[1748736000,-3.58],[1751328000,-8.64],[1754006400,10.13],[1756684800,-0.01],[1759276800,-4.76],[1761955200,-0.19],[1764547200,-2.63],[1767225600,-1.36],[1769904000,6.24],[1772323200,1.47],[1775001600,-1.62],[1777593600,3.35],[1780272000,6.99],[1782864000,18.1],[1785542400,5.48],[1788220800,13.24]]}],"frequency":"M"}],"qna":[{"question":"What does this measure?","answer":"Raw coal (coking and non-coking) produced and despatched in the month, in million tonnes (MT), by Coal India Ltd and its subsidiaries, Singareni Collieries Company Ltd and captive/commercial mines. Lignite is reported separately by the Ministry and is not included.^'Production' is output at the pit head; 'despatch' is coal moved out by rail, road, MGR and other modes to consumers."},{"question":"How should I read it?","answer":"Use the YoY view. Growth in despatch above production means stock is being drawn down. Coal despatch to the power sector rises with electricity demand and falls when hydro and renewables are abundant (monsoon months). Captive and commercial mines are the fastest-growing segment, so compare CIL on its own for the legacy trend."},{"question":"Definitions, revisions and caveats","answer":"Each monthly PDF is provisional and also gives the same month of the previous year (revised). The series uses the provisional figure for the latest months and the revised figure once a later PDF restates it, so recent months can be revised slightly.^Months before mid-2021 are not available from these PDFs. The parser checks that the three producers add to the grand total and that growth rates quoted in the PDF match the numbers."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:11:31+00:00"}